00:29:17.520 --> 00:29:21.630
with confidence about
the data, and really,

00:29:21.630 --> 00:29:27.540
you should not expect any
surprises when moving an app

00:29:27.540 --> 00:29:30.990
from development to production
because it's built right

00:29:30.990 --> 00:29:33.180
from the start on
the same foundation.

00:29:33.180 --> 00:29:36.210
That's exactly
what we want here.

00:29:36.210 --> 00:29:40.590
We've seen how quick and easy we
can create new enterprise-ready

00:29:40.590 --> 00:29:42.690
applications with Rayfin.

00:29:42.690 --> 00:29:47.400
The question that naturally
comes next is how we can use the

00:29:47.400 --> 00:29:52.290
data that our app generated
to build dynamic dashboards

00:29:52.290 --> 00:29:57.250
to get insights, because,
yes, there's more to Rayfin.

00:29:58.740 --> 00:30:01.410
The idea here is pretty simple.

00:30:01.410 --> 00:30:05.550
Instead of treating the app
and the analytics experience

00:30:05.550 --> 00:30:10.320
as two separate worlds, we can
bring them closer together.

00:30:10.320 --> 00:30:14.340
We can do that using the new
analytics app templates that's

00:30:14.340 --> 00:30:15.990
built for Rayfin.

00:30:15.990 --> 00:30:19.200
Currently, the Analytics
app can work seamlessly

00:30:19.200 --> 00:30:20.220
with semantic models,

00:30:20.220 --> 00:30:24.210
so the data your app produces
can immediately be displayed

00:30:24.210 --> 00:30:25.440
on a dashboard.

00:30:25.440 --> 00:30:29.100
On top of that, you get
a robust visual stack,

00:30:29.100 --> 00:30:32.190
not just basic charts, but
a complete design skill

00:30:32.190 --> 00:30:35.760
for AI agents that
help turn raw data

00:30:35.760 --> 00:30:37.770
into something that's
more polished,

00:30:37.770 --> 00:30:40.680
readable, and useful to you.

00:30:40.680 --> 00:30:42.750
For developers,
this is really nice

00:30:42.750 --> 00:30:46.680
because you're not just building
an app and saying good luck

00:30:46.680 --> 00:30:48.540
to the business afterwards.

00:30:48.540 --> 00:30:51.870
You're building an experience
where the data can flow directly

00:30:51.870 --> 00:30:56.550
into dashboards,
reportings, and insights.

00:30:56.550 --> 00:30:59.430
Yeah, there's also more
coming soon as the experience

00:30:59.430 --> 00:31:02.250
to define custom
actions triggered

00:31:02.250 --> 00:31:06.480
by your data will become simpler
and even more integrated.

00:31:06.480 --> 00:31:10.770
Let's have a quick look at what
it means for our chef app.

